# 1. The Big Picture

Many beginners think these are separate concepts:

- Containerfile
- Image
- Container
- Volume Mounts
- Systemd
- Rootless Containers
- Auto-start

In reality, they are simply **different stages of one workflow.**

```text
Containerfile
      │
      ▼
podman build
      │
      ▼
Image
      │
      ▼
podman run
      │
      ▼
Container
      │
      ▼
podman generate systemd
      │
      ▼
systemctl --user enable
      │
      ▼
Automatic Startup
```

> **Everything starts with an Image.**

---

# 2. Image = Blueprint

An **Image** is **NOT** a running container.

Think of it as a blueprint or template.

```text
                Image
                  │
      ┌───────────┼───────────┐
      ▼           ▼           ▼
 Container1   Container2   Container3
```

One image can create **unlimited containers.**

Example:

```bash
podman run --name web1 myimage
podman run --name web2 myimage
podman run --name web3 myimage
```

Notice:

- Same image
- Multiple containers
- Image never changes

