# 11. Rootless Containers

A rootless container is simply a container owned by a **regular user** instead of root.

Example users:

```
natasha
maria
harry
walhalla
```

Systemd service location:

```
~/.config/systemd/user/
```

instead of:

```
/etc/systemd/system/
```

Benefits:

- No root privileges required
- Better security
- Preferred in RHCSA EX200

---

# 12. EX200 Container Workflow

Almost every Podman question in EX200 follows this exact pattern.

```text
Login as User
      │
      ▼
Run Container
      │
      ▼
Generate systemd Service
      │
      ▼
Move Service File
(~/.config/systemd/user/)
      │
      ▼
systemctl --user daemon-reload
      │
      ▼
systemctl --user enable --now
      │
      ▼
loginctl enable-linger USER
      │
      ▼
Verify
```

Only these values change:

- Image Name
- Container Name
- Username
- Host Directory
- Container Directory
- Service Name

The workflow never changes.

---

# 13. Relationship Between Components

```text
Containerfile
        │
        ▼
   Build Image
        │
        ▼
      Image
        │
 ┌──────┼─────────────┐
 ▼      ▼             ▼
Container1      Container2      Container3
```

Remember:

- One Image → Many Containers
- One Container → Cannot become an Image automatically

If required:

```bash
podman commit
```

creates a new image from a container.

